golden -h

-- exit status: 1 --
-- stderr --
usage: golden [-D <name>[=<value>] ...] [-i] <out.golden> <cmd> [<args>...]
       golden [-u] <in.golden>

With 2 or more arguments, golden captures the output of the given command and
writes it to the given golden file.
With exactly 1 argument, golden replays the given golden file and asserts that
the command's output matches the captured one.

  -i    capture stdin ([i]nteractive)
  -D    capture environment variable `<name>[=<value>]`
        If just a name is given, the value is taken from the environment.
  -u    update: replay and overwrite with the new output
